  "carriedObservations": {},
  "rootAssessment": "Substantive lead assent to seven separately verified D5 units: production build-script roots, nonempty path proofs and explicit non-exempt rootless regions preserve exact spawn/environment ownership; the future launcher execve exception stays empty until accepted D1b ownership. Codec fakes require frame replay and executable smoke controls; release waits retain law constants; actual concurrency resolver values and genuine overlap determine evidence credit. POSIX setsid failures receive no confinement credit; per-attempt validity and explicit operational outcome sets remain. D3b, D4, Rust3, resolver, CF/D1b and Linux dependencies stay open until their own accepted work. Acceptance of this plan supplies no implementation, runtime or qualification result.",
  "rulings": {
    "Q11": "ACCEPT: gated exemptions now require a nonempty resolved and satisfiable root path; every in-scope rootless region is non-exempt or fails the structural check; and a separate build = false control requires both owner tools to refuse forbidden spawn and extra environment-read sites in otherwise-unreachable build.rs and helper files while preserving the mixed-path case."
